{
  "root_cause": "htmlParseHTMLAttribute (and its caller htmlParseAttValue) dereferenced the CUR/NXT macros without first ensuring ctxt->input->cur was still within the valid input buffer. When the input buffer was empty/at EOF (or after error recovery/buffer growth failures), CUR evaluated *(ctxt->input->cur) one byte past the end of a 1-byte global string, triggering a 1-byte global out-of-bounds read.",
  "fix_approach": "Make CUR/NXT uses in the vulnerable attribute parsing path bounds-aware with minimal local guards: (1) tighten htmlParseHTMLAttribute’s main loop condition to require a valid input pointer and ctxt->input->cur < ctxt->input->end before evaluating CUR, and guard the NXT(1) lookahead with an explicit (cur+1 < end) check; (2) add early safety checks in htmlParseAttValue to ensure input pointers are valid and not at/after end before using CUR, and after parsing quoted attributes, GROW and check cur<end before reading CUR to test for the closing quote. This prevents the one-byte OOB read while preserving existing parsing behavior.",
  "files_modified": [
    "HTMLparser.c"
  ],
